# Build output and per-machine state for the Android project.
#
# Without this the folder is ~180MB of compiled classes, merged resources and
# Gradle caches — all of it regenerated by a build, none of it worth a diff.
# What stays tracked is the source, the manifests, the resources and the
# Gradle build files: everything Android Studio needs to rebuild from clean.

# Gradle's own working state and the build products of every module.
.gradle/
build/

# The SDK path on this particular machine. The file says so itself, and it
# would send the next person's build looking for a directory they don't have.
local.properties

# Android Studio / IntelliJ project state. Which panes were open, which file
# was focused, per-machine JDK paths — rewritten constantly, shared by nobody.
.idea/
*.iml

# Native build scratch, only present if a module ever adds C/C++.
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/

# Screenshots and profiling captures taken from the IDE.
/captures/
